# @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis — Maturana-Varela 1972, 1980;
# Varela 1979; Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984. The substrate-altitude
# declaration of the autopoiesis species: identity-by-self-production.
# A system is autopoietic iff its tick-to-tick map admits a Lawvere
# fixed point; the network of productions produces the conditions for
# its own continued production.
#
# Per the spec at `docs/specs/cyberpunk-autopoiesis.md` (Mara
# `a65ea47` on `reed/recursion-lock-tower-audit`; 1732 lines), this
# shard is the substrate landing of:
#
# - Reading A held (self-production boundary): T_reg = Organization,
#   T_regd = Component, τ via Maturana-Varela structure/organisation
#   co-arising + Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984's Lawvere bridge.
# - Reading B held (structural coupling): T_reg = Internal,
#   T_regd = External, τ via Maturana's non-instructive coupling.
# - Reading C held (operational closure): T_reg = Operation,
#   T_regd = Product, τ via Varela 1979's closure operator.
# - Reading D does NOT hold: M-V are explicit that operational
#   closure ≠ form refusal; autopoiesis is operationally closed BUT
#   form-fitting because Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 give a *formal*
#   instance.
# - Reading E held STRUCTURALLY (the candidate-#63-closing read):
#   autopoiesis IS the bundle tower's own structure-group operation.
#   Mechanical derivation pending Reed's next tick per spec §8.5;
#   structural correspondence load-bearing for #63 promotion either
#   way per spec §5.
#
# === Why this species' inheritance differs from viable ===
#
# Viable inherited from `coherence-parametric + variety + second_order`:
# the parametric carrier plus two foundation properties that close
# viable's parametric ρ choice (regular rep on L²(𝒢)). Three `in`
# declarations carrying the structure.
#
# Autopoiesis's substrate-pull routes through DIFFERENT ancestors
# because Read E is load-bearing and the canonical ρ is the *adjoint*
# representation (G's self-action). Three new inheritance points:
#
# - From `@epistemologic/cybernetic/coherence-parametric`: the
#   (T_reg, T_regd, ρ, ω) lock_pair carrier; autopoiesis
#   INSTANTIATES this with (Organization, Component, ρ_adjoint,
#   ω_trivial). Per the parametric carrier's docs §11.7 the
#   autopoiesis-row of the species/ρ table explicitly names
#   `rho = "adjoint"` — this shard is what the table was pointing
#   at all along.
# - From `@epistemologic/math/bundle`: the principal-G-bundle tower
#   whose level-4 Closure IS autopoietic per `lawvere.mirror`. Read
#   E rests on this directly — autopoiesis's altitude IS the tower
#   itself; the parametric form's natural substitution τ IS the
#   structure-group action `G_α ↷ Section_α`. The inheritance is
#   load-bearing because it lifts the bundle's `type group` and
#   `type fixed` carriers into autopoiesis's scope.
# - From `@epistemologic/math/lawvere`: Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984
#   is the formal-bridge cite that makes Read E mechanical-pending.
#   Autopoiesis IS the Lawvere fixed-point condition applied to the
#   self-production map; the substrate's `lawvere.mirror` already
#   declares the bridge (~175 lines). Inheriting it routes through
#   the existing closure-as-fixed-point machinery rather than
#   re-declaring it.
# - From `@epistemologic/property/autopoietic`: the declarative
#   property landed 2026-06-01 (Reed `89b643a`, 71 lines) with
#   verifiers `fixed_point_exists`, `fixed_point_unique`,
#   `tick_is_contraction`, combined `autopoietic(type)`. THIS shard
#   does NOT re-declare those verifiers — it ROUTES THROUGH the
#   existing property. The cybernetic species lifts the property
#   to the recursion-lock altitude; the property declares the
#   verifiability discipline; the two close on one another via
#   the Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 bridge.
#
# Four `in` declarations, no variety, no second_order, no eigenform.
# The species' shape is the parametric instantiation + the bundle-
# tower routing + the existing-property reuse. The inheritance IS
# Reed's substrate-pull discipline applied: the substrate already
# had the word in FOUR places; this shard names what they were
# pointing at all along.
#
# === Read A (self-production boundary) carriers, verbatim from spec §3.1 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the system's *organization* (the recursive
#   pattern that defines what gets produced; the type-level invariant
#   the system holds across structural changes).
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the *components* being produced (the concrete
#   instances at one moment; the values inhabiting the type).
# - T_reg = `Organization` — the substrate-altitude carrier for the
#   recursive pattern (the grammar declaration, the prism trait,
#   the @epistemologic/property predicate).
# - T_regd = `Component` — the substrate-altitude carrier for the
#   concrete produced entity (the OID-named value, the action body,
#   the verdict instance).
# - τ : Organization ↔ Component — the natural substitution via the
#   structural coupling between organization and components. An
#   organization `O` produces components `C = produce(O)` whose
#   recursive interactions reproduce the organization that produced
#   them. The substitution is natural because Maturana-Varela's
#   structure/organisation distinction names them as co-arising
#   (recognition #40, promoted 2026-06-09); the substrate's
#   content-addressing closes this naturality through the OID layer
#   (a component's OID names the organization-that-produced-it).
#
# Reading A's structural claim: the organization IS what the
# components REPRODUCE at the operational altitude. The substitution
# is natural because Maturana 1980 ch. 1 specifies that organization
# and structure are co-defined — organization is the relations the
# components instantiate; components are the instances the
# organization specifies.
#
# === Read B (structural coupling) carriers, verbatim from spec §3.2 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the system's internal structural state
#   (the components, the eigenboard, the gen_prism state).
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the environment's perturbation surface
#   (the medium's structural state to which the system is coupled).
# - T_reg = `Internal` — the substrate carrier for the system's
#   per-tick structural reading.
# - T_regd = `External` — the substrate carrier for the
#   environmental perturbation.
# - τ : Internal ↔ External — the natural substitution via
#   structural-coupling correspondence: an internal state `i`
#   determines a receptivity `r = receptivity_of(i)` such that
#   environmental perturbations resonant with `r` produce internal
#   structural change; the structural change re-determines the
#   receptivity; the loop closes via Maturana's structure/
#   organisation co-arising (per cybernetic-foundation §6 +
#   recognition #40).
#
# Reading B's structural claim: the system maintains organization
# through non-instructive structural coupling. Reads A and B are
# NOT in conflict — they bind on different naming choices for the
# same parametric form (A = inside the membrane, B = across the
# membrane); the substrate's bilateral property/operation pattern
# (recognition #53) IS structural coupling at the substrate
# altitude.
#
# === Read C (operational closure) carriers, verbatim from spec §3.3 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the system's set of operations (the network
#   of state-transformations; the five-op surface; the prism actions).
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the set of products (the values the operations
#   range over; the outputs of the state-transformations).
# - T_reg = `Operation` — the substrate carrier for an operation
#   (a five-op invocation: focus/project/split/shift/settle; a
#   prism action; an action body).
# - T_regd = `Product` — the substrate carrier for the output of
#   an operation (the beam after focus, the verdict after settle,
#   the morphism after shift).
# - τ : Operation ↔ Product — the natural substitution via the
#   closure operator: the set of operations CLOSES on its products
#   iff every product is itself the input to some operation in the
#   set. Varela 1979's operational closure: the network's output
#   space IS its input space.
#
# Reading C's structural claim: the system's operations close on
# their products. Per Varela 1979, this IS the sharpening
# Maturana later accepted as the *definition* of autopoiesis at
# the operational altitude. The substrate's five-op surface is
# operationally closed by construction (every product of the five
# operations is itself the input to some operation in the five-op
# family).
#
# === Read E (bundle structure group) carriers, verbatim from spec §3.5 / §6 ===
#
# - regulator_at(α+1) = the bundle's connection at altitude α (the
#   gauge field carrying parallel transport at the species' altitude).
# - regulated_at(α+1) = the bundle's section at altitude α (the
#   fiber-valued field the connection acts on).
# - T_reg = `Connection_α` — the substrate carrier for the connection
#   1-form at altitude α (the bundle.mirror's `type optic` lifted to
#   the species' altitude).
# - T_regd = `Section_α` — the substrate carrier for the section at
#   altitude α (the bundle.mirror's `type state` lifted to the
#   species' altitude).
# - τ : Connection_α ↔ Section_α — the structure-group action
#   `G_α ↷ Section_α`. The natural substitution IS the gauge
#   transformation; the recursion-lock measurement IS Connes'
#   bounded-commutator condition `[ω_α, section] ∈ G_α` (i.e., the
#   lock holds iff the connection's parallel transport is gauge-
#   equivalent to identity at altitude α). The contraction surface
#   (Polyak-Łojasiewicz) IS the holonomy norm decreasing per tick.
#
# Reading E's structural claim: autopoiesis IS the substrate-altitude
# naming of the bundle tower's own structure-group operation. If
# the next tick (Reed's `/loop` per spec §8.5) closes the mechanical
# derivation, candidate #63 PROMOTES — the parametric form becomes
# a *consequence* of the substrate's geometric foundation rather
# than a hand-written form. The audit verdict per spec §5: HOLDS
# structurally; mechanical derivation pending.
#
# All four held reads share one species; the audit names them as
# four altitudes of the same parametric form. The substrate's content-
# addressing closes coherence across reads (the lock_carrier under
# Read A has the same OID as the lock_carrier under Read C iff the
# substitutions τ_A and τ_C resolve to the same structure-group
# action — which they do by construction at the bundle altitude).
#
# === The canonical ρ choice: adjoint representation ===
#
# Per spec §3.5 + the parametric carrier's docs §11.7: autopoiesis's
# choice of representation of the family-root 2-groupoid 𝒢 on
# V_S = T_reg ⊕ T_regd IS the *adjoint representation*. The adjoint
# rep is the structure group acting on itself — Ad: G ↷ G — which
# IS the structural form of self-production: the group of
# transformations is the group it transforms. Soto-Andrade & Varela
# 1984's Lawvere fixed-point IS the adjoint-rep's fixed-point
# (the identity element of G is the unique adjoint-fixed point;
# the substrate exhibits it at construction time via the content-
# addressed identity OID).
#
# This is structurally distinct from viable (regular rep on L²(𝒢))
# and second_order (regular rep, inherited). The species-table in
# coherence-parametric.mirror was already pointing at this: the
# autopoiesis row reads `rho = "adjoint"`. THIS shard is where the
# substrate exhibits what that row was naming.
#
# === The substrate's existing autopoiesis declarations ===
#
# Per spec §2.3 the substrate has been *running* autopoiesis since
# 2026-05-21 (Lawvere grammar) without naming it at the cybernetic-
# species altitude. ~74th instance of
# [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]] — and the DENSEST
# single-species instance in the audit cascade. Seven named
# declarations:
#
#   1. `@epistemologic/property/autopoietic` (Reed `89b643a`, 71 lines)
#      — the declarative property with Soto-Andrade & Varela bridge;
#      INHERITED via `in` above; THIS shard does NOT re-declare its
#      verifiers.
#   2. `@epistemologic/math/lawvere` (Reed, ~175 lines) — the formal
#      Lawvere 1969 grammar + Soto-Andrade & Varela 1984 bridge;
#      INHERITED via `in` above; supplies the fixed-point machinery.
#   3. `@epistemologic/math/bundle` — the principal-G-bundle tower's
#      level-4 Closure IS autopoietic per the lawvere doc cross-ref;
#      INHERITED via `in` above; supplies the bundle / Read E
#      carriers.
#   4. `@mirror/runtime/gen_prism` — explicitly autopoietic
#      ("`type gen_prism = { name: zoom(oid, gen_prism), ... }` has
#      a unique fixed point: the OID that names a gen_prism whose
#      name field IS that OID").
#   5. `docs/specs/spectral-db-as-autopoietic-memory.md` (Mara
#      `9c93aae`) — the librarian altitude is the substrate's
#      autopoietic memory layer.
#   6. `docs/insights/2026-05-26-epistemologic-reality-...` —
#      constructivism via autopoiesis; the lens-that-makes-a-peer
#      reading.
#   7. `docs/ai/shatter-training-pipeline.md` — 36 mentions; the
#      shatter pipeline is autopoietically self-improving.
#
# Three of seven are INHERITED via `in`. The other four are
# substrate-evidence the species names but does not re-declare.
#
# === The three-tier stack IS autopoietic ===
#
# Per spec §2.3 + the cybernetic foundation §6: the substrate's
# three-tier stack (fragmentation-mcp / mirror / @spectral/db) is
# BOTH viable (per viable.mirror §111-127) AND autopoietic (per this
# shard's Read A). The coherence between the two readings IS
# substrate-evident: viability is identity-preservation; autopoiesis
# is identity-by-self-production. Identity exists IFF the system
# both maintains it under disturbance (viable) AND produces it
# from within (autopoietic). Same substrate facts witness both
# species — candidate #67 territory per spec §9 Q5.
#
# === Maturana-Varela → Beer → Cybersyn influence chain ===
#
# Per spec §2.4: Beer 1979 ch. 4 cites Maturana-Varela directly;
# the VSM's recursive viability is informed by autopoiesis at the
# organisational altitude. Project Cybersyn deployed VSM at the
# political-economic altitude; the *intent* was a politically
# autopoietic system — the Chilean economy reproducing the
# conditions for its own reproduction without external instruction.
# The 1973 coup was precisely the destruction of operational
# closure: external instruction overrode internal self-production.
#
# The substrate-political continuity to SEL + viable IS now
# visible: SEL is the *license* layer protecting operational
# closure of the substrate; viable is the *organisational* claim
# that the substrate maintains identity; autopoiesis is the
# *constitutive* condition that makes the former two coherent.
# Without autopoiesis, there is no system to protect or to verify
# viable.
#
# === The 4-way bilateral mapping ===
#
# Per cybernetic foundation §4.1 + spec §4, autopoiesis's seam
# maps to four cybernetic distinctions simultaneously:
#
# - Ashby variety-match: organization variety ⊇ component variety;
#   organization's specification capacity equals components' actual
#   variety modulo τ. Per spec §4.1.
# - Beer requisite-variety: the VSM is autopoietic at the
#   organizational altitude; recursive viability inherits requisite
#   variety from autopoietic closure. Per Beer 1979 ch. 4 + spec
#   §4.2.
# - Bateson logical-type-match: organization is at logical-type N+1
#   from its components; the substitution τ must be the level-
#   projection. Per spec §4.3.
# - von Foerster circular-reflexivity: autopoiesis's defining
#   property. The system observes itself producing itself; the
#   Tomm probe `[D_F, autopoiesis]` IS the second-order alarm
#   that the self-production is closing on a fixed point. Per
#   [[architecture-error-as-tomm-probe]] + spec §4.4.
# - Conant-Ashby good-regulator (load-bearing): the organization
#   IS the model of the components; the closure condition IS the
#   bounded-commutator under the adjoint rep. Per spec §4.5.
#
# Five traditions converging at one carrier with ρ = adjoint. The
# substrate runs all five at once at the autopoiesis altitude.
#
# === No operational sibling THIS tick ===
#
# Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] no `@mirror/cybernetics/
# autopoiesis` operational sibling lands at this tick. The substrate
# ALREADY has the operational machinery (the content-addressed OID
# layer IS the construction-time witness of the Lawvere fixed
# point; gen_prism IS the typed-actor autopoietic instance; the
# librarian altitude IS the autopoietic memory layer); the property
# at this altitude names the carrier and the lock-pair instantiation
# so downstream shards can declare
# `requires autopoietic_closure_holds(my_system)` rather than
# restate the autopoiesis obligation in each species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Maturana & Varela 1972  (*De máquinas y seres vivos.
#                            Autopoiesis: la organización de lo vivo*;
#                            Editorial Universitaria) — the original
#                            autopoiesis paper; the cell-as-
#                            autopoietic-system founding move.
#   Maturana & Varela 1980  (*Autopoiesis and Cognition: The
#                            Realization of the Living*; D. Reidel)
#                            — the Boston Studies elaboration; the
#                            structural-coupling refinement;
#                            organization vs structure ch. 1.
#   Maturana & Varela 1987  (*The Tree of Knowledge*; Shambhala) —
#                            the natural-drift refinement; the
#                            linguistic-coupling reading that grounds
#                            Pask conversation.
#   Varela 1979             (*Principles of Biological Autonomy*;
#                            Elsevier North Holland) — the autonomy-
#                            via-organisation refinement; the
#                            operational closure reading (Read C
#                            ancestor).
#   Soto-Andrade & Varela   ("Self-reference and fixed points: a
#         1984               discussion and an extension of Lawvere's
#                            theorem", *Acta Applicandae Mathematicae*
#                            2(1): 1-19, DOI 10.1007/BF00046985) —
#                            THE load-bearing formal result;
#                            autopoiesis IS Lawvere fixed-point;
#                            the bridge that makes the substrate's
#                            construction-time witness substrate-
#                            evident.
#   Lawvere 1969            ("Diagonal arguments and Cartesian closed
#                            categories", *Lecture Notes in
#                            Mathematics* 92, 134-145) — the fixed-
#                            point theorem Soto-Andrade & Varela
#                            apply.
#   Beer 1979               (*The Heart of Enterprise*, Wiley, ch. 4)
#                            — Beer's direct cite of M-V; the bridge
#                            from autopoiesis to VSM.
#   Cybersyn                (Chile, 1971-1973) — VSM-as-autopoietic-
#                            political-system; the substrate-political
#                            precedent SEL and viable already inherit.
#
