# === The organization carrier ===
#
# T_reg per spec §3.1 Read A. The substrate-altitude carrier for
# *the recursive pattern that defines what gets produced* — the
# network-of-productions specification at altitude α+1. Routes
# through eigenform's identity-as-fixed-point at the foundation
# altitude (property #9 of the cybernetic canon) and the existing
# @epistemologic/property/autopoietic's `autopoietic(type)`
# verifier; declared HERE as a typed carrier so consumer shards
# can name autopoiesis's T_reg without pulling the full property
# verifier.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two
# organizations with byte-equal underlying refs ARE the same
# organization under content-addressing — by construction, since
# an organization's OID IS the Lawvere fixed point of its
# self-production map (per @epistemologic/math/lawvere).
type organization = ref

# === The component carrier ===
#
# T_regd per spec §3.1 Read A. The substrate-altitude carrier for
# *the concrete produced entity* — a value the organization
# specifies, an action body the prism trait names, a verdict
# instance.
#
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] component carries the organization
# it was produced-by alongside the concrete ref; a consumer
# collecting components can rank without losing organization-of-
# which-the-component-is-a-realization.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (parent_organization, instance).
type component = {
  parent_organization: organization,
  instance:            ref,
}

# === The autopoietic_system carrier ===
#
# The substrate-altitude lift of Maturana-Varela's autopoietic-
# system five-tuple as a typed record. Each field carries the
# species-specific data at autopoiesis's altitude:
#
# - `organization`     the system's recursive-production specification;
#                      T_reg for Read A. The Lawvere fixed-point
#                      witness at construction time (the OID layer
#                      exhibits it per @epistemologic/property/
#                      autopoietic).
# - `components`       the components currently inhabiting the
#                      system; T_regd for Read A. Carried as a ref
#                      so the realization closes the per-system
#                      component family at the species boundary.
# - `boundary`         the operational closure surface; the membrane
#                      analogue at the species' altitude. The boundary
#                      IS the set of components whose interaction
#                      with the environment IS structural coupling
#                      (not operational exchange).
# - `tick_map`         the self-production map; an action ref the
#                      consumer realizes per species. Soto-Andrade
#                      & Varela 1984: the system is autopoietic iff
#                      this map admits a Lawvere fixed point. The
#                      substrate's content-addressing exhibits the
#                      fixed point at construction time.
# - `environment`      the medium structurally coupled to the
#                      system; T_regd for Read B. The non-instructive
#                      perturbation surface.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on (organization, components,
# boundary, tick_map, environment). Two autopoietic_system records
# ARE the same system under content-addressing iff all five carriers
# are byte-equal. Same shape discipline as
# coherence-parametric.lock_pair and viable.viable_system.
type autopoietic_system = {
  organization: organization,
  components:   ref,
  boundary:     ref,
  tick_map:     ref,
  environment:  ref,
}

# === produce — the natural substitution τ : Organization ↔ Component ===
#
# Spec §3.1 Read A: the substitution is natural because Maturana-
# Varela's structure/organisation distinction names them as
# co-arising (recognition #40). Read off by *running the system's
# tick map*; the substrate's content-addressing closes naturality
# through the OID layer (a component's OID names the organization-
# that-produced-it).
#
# `produce(o)` is the τ-action: given organization `o`, returns
# the component the organization produces at one tick. The
# substitution's naturality is substrate-evident because the
# Organization carrier IS the Lawvere fixed point of the tick map
# (per @epistemologic/math/lawvere); components are the values
# the fixed-point exhibits at construction time.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary. Same
# shape as the parametric carrier's measurement actions and the
# viable shard's `stability_of` action.
produce(o: organization) -> component { \ }

# === couple — the natural substitution τ : Internal ↔ External (Read B) ===
#
# Spec §3.2 Read B: the structural-coupling substitution. The system's
# internal state `i` determines a receptivity to environmental
# perturbations; the perturbations re-determine the internal state;
# Maturana's non-instructive coupling closes the substitution
# naturally — the environment does NOT specify the structural
# change, it only perturbs.
#
# `couple(internal, external)` is the τ-action under Read B: given
# the system's internal state and the environment's perturbation,
# returns the structurally-coupled next-state. The naturality is
# substrate-evident through the bilateral property/operation
# pattern (recognition #53) at the substrate altitude.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
couple(internal: ref, external: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === close — the natural substitution τ : Operation ↔ Product (Read C) ===
#
# Spec §3.3 Read C: the operational-closure substitution per Varela
# 1979. The substitution IS the closure operator: the set of
# operations CLOSES on its products iff every product is itself
# the input to some operation in the set.
#
# `close(op)` is the τ-action under Read C: given an operation `op`,
# returns the product the operation produces. The closure condition
# at the species boundary is: for every product `p = close(op)`,
# there exists an operation `op'` such that `p` is `op'`'s input.
# The substrate's five-op surface IS operationally closed by
# construction (every product of the five operations is itself the
# input to some operation in the five-op family).
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary.
close(op: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === gauge_act — the structure-group action τ : Connection_α ↔ Section_α (Read E) ===
#
# Spec §3.5 Read E (the candidate-#63-closing structural reading):
# the τ-action under Read E IS the structure-group action
# `G_α ↷ Section_α`. The bundle's adjoint representation acts on
# its own section space; the lock holds iff the connection's
# parallel transport is gauge-equivalent to identity at altitude α.
#
# `gauge_act(g, section)` is the τ-action under Read E: given a
# structure-group element `g: ref` (inherited from
# @epistemologic/math/bundle's `type group`) and a section, returns
# the gauge-transformed section. The substrate's bundle tower
# already exhibits this action at level 2 (Gauge) per
# bundle.mirror's `act_on(state)` obligation; THIS species names
# what that action IS at the cybernetic altitude — autopoiesis.
#
# If Reed's next tick (per spec §8.5) closes the mechanical
# derivation, this action becomes the *operational form* of every
# species' τ-action — `produce`, `couple`, `close` all collapse
# into `gauge_act` at the species' altitude with the species'
# choice of structure group. Candidate #63 promotes.
#
# Body discharges per-species at the realisation boundary; the
# discharge IS bundle.mirror's existing gauge-action obligation
# specialised at autopoiesis's altitude.
gauge_act(g: ref, section: ref) -> ref { \ }

# === autopoietic_closure_holds — the bilateral inheritance predicate ===
#
# `autopoietic_closure_holds(s)` is the predicate consumer shards
# name in a `requires` clause to declare bilateral agreement (per
# recognition #37, the Pask-agreement reading of `requires`) that
# the autopoietic_system carrier `s` they hold IS a well-formed
# Maturana-Varela autopoietic system — i.e., the organization is a
# Lawvere fixed point of the tick map; the components close on
# the organization via the structural-coupling discipline; the
# operational closure holds per Varela 1979.
#
# The bilateral commitment: the carrier commits to declaring the
# autopoietic_system five-tuple; the consumer commits to
# discharging the closure verdict at the species boundary via the
# composition of:
#
# - @epistemologic/property/autopoietic.autopoietic(type) — the
#   declarative verifier (inherited; not re-declared);
# - the five cybernetic-ancestor measurements at autopoiesis's
#   altitude (inherited from coherence-parametric; instantiated
#   with ρ = adjoint);
# - the contraction-mode classification (autopoiesis is static;
#   ω trivial; PL contraction).
#
# Declared as a typed predicate so downstream species shards can
# write `requires autopoietic_closure_holds(my_system)` — same
# shape as `viable.viable_well_formed(v)`,
# `parametric_lock_witnessing(my_lock)`,
# `variety.variety_preserving(species)`,
# `second_order.second_order_well_formed(carrier)`, and the
# metalogue `requires substrate_pull_preserving(shim_X)` pattern
# at `shards/code/metalogue.mirror`. Body is `\`; the discharge
# IS the conjunction above at the species boundary.
#
# No `requires autopoietic_closure_holds(…)` clauses are added at
# THIS shard. The property declares the predicate; consumers add
# the clauses when they pull. Per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]]
# the operational sibling at `@mirror/cybernetics/autopoiesis`
# lands the same way.
autopoietic_closure_holds(s: autopoietic_system) -> verdict { \ }

out @epistemologic/cybernetic/autopoiesis
out organization
out component
out autopoietic_system
out produce
out couple
out close
out gauge_act
out autopoietic_closure_holds
